    "abstract": "We investigate environmental stigmergy within the Boids Hunter multi-temporal artificial life system. When autonomous player entities fail, their terminal spatial coordinates deposit permanent repulsive forcefield nodes into the shared substrate. We show that subsequent boid swarms undergo statistically significant trajectory deflections (mean centroid shift = 208.4px, p < 0.001) without direct peer-to-peer communication channels, proving coordination across disconnected execution turns.",
